      "text": "The Gas Safety (Installation and Use) Regulations 1998 require landlords to arrange an annual gas safety check by a Gas Safe registered engineer and to record the result. The engineer completes the record correctly; the landlord obtains, retains, and provides it. Failure can mean a fine, an improvement notice, or prosecution by the HSE."
